      "writtenOn": "2019-06-20T19:12:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you\u0027re right there\u0027s a grey are where the decision is difficult. There\u0027s cases where it\u0027s clear that dumping stack is not necessary, for example if we\u0027re sure the user made a human error in supplying invalid input. There\u0027s cases where we know we should dump stack, for example an assertion that\u0027s not supposed to trigger, or an error coming from a lower-level library that we don\u0027t know how to handle. For things in the middle I think we\u0027ll just need to use our best judgement.",
